From 30236f14c60b0fe6adfe1561b970cf4de2b44978 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Christopher Owen <christopherowen@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 08:40:50 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat(dspark): online verification-driven drafter adaptation

Base: 15833ed19c5d (candidate-54 patch 0799, tree ad2dc11f613f)
Rationale: DSpark's confidence head is calibrated online by
  OnlineAcceptanceEstimator's shared-slope refit every 100 steps, and its
  Markov W1 and confidence head never learn from verification. This adds three
  opt-in parts, off unless their variables are set:
  - VLLM_DSPARK_ONLINE_CALIBRATION (or VLLM_DSPARK_ONLINE_ADAPT): a
    per-position log-odds calibrator (scale and bias per draft position, FP64,
    updated every step from the accepted and first-rejected positions) takes
    the place of the estimator's refit in the captured draft graph's
    calibration kernel (PER_POSITION_SLOPE).
  - VLLM_DSPARK_ONLINE_ADAPT: DSparkOnlineAdaptation grades each draft with
    the next step's verification (observe_verification now receives the
    sampled tokens) and takes a prefix-product total-variation (E2E-TV) plus
    confidence BCE step on the replicated Markov W1 and the confidence head.
    The support at each verified position is the target's token, the draft
    and one other id; the drafter's base and Markov logits there come from
    the vocabulary shards (VocabRows: the rank owning an id contributes its
    row, the others zeros, one all-reduce sums them exactly), so W2 and the LM
    head are never indexed by global ids on a shard. The draft step keeps the
    head hidden rows, anchors and request slots it needs (capture, inside the
    graph); only a real draft step is graded (arm). Copy-drafted rows are
    skipped. W2 is never written under TP or when packed
    (VLLM_DSPARK_ONLINE_UPDATE_W2 is refused there). Each touched W1 row stays
    within VLLM_DSPARK_ONLINE_MAX_DRIFT (default 1.0) of its loaded norm, and
    reset() restores the loaded heads. VLLM_DSPARK_ONLINE_DIGEST_STEPS logs a
    bit digest of the adapted state per rank.
  - VLLM_DSPARK_SESSION_MEMORY_TOKENS: CopyDrafter's fallback ring of a
    request's own verified tokens, per request slot and cleared with the slot.
Quality: the target's verification alone decides the emitted tokens, so no
  part changes the text; they change the drafts and the verified rows. Every
  update reads only inputs identical on all TP ranks and reduces in a fixed
  order without atomics, so ranks keep identical drafter state. Off by
  default: with the variables unset nothing is allocated or launched.
Tests: pytest tests/v1/spec_decode/test_online_dspark_adaptation.py (13
  passed on GB10, with the DS4.1 checkpoint's heads): shard mapping of global
  ids, W2 update refusal, four gloo ranks bit-identical and equal to one rank
  on DS4.1's sharded W2 and LM head, only armed observed DSpark positions
  update, the drift bound and reset, the closed-form E2E-TV step against
  autograd, the calibrator driving the estimator, the Triton kernel's
  per-position slope, packed rows of a real shard against BF16 rows, GPU
  run-to-run identity, per-request session rings. The spec-decode suites
  (acceptance estimator, adaptive verification, copy drafts, DSpark top-k,
  gathered Markov, vocabulary parallel, greedy Markov, utils, autoregressive
  speculator): 247 passed, 1 skipped; the 2 failures of test_dspark_topk.py's
  test_dspark_revisited_position_uses_step_seed fail alike on candidate-54.
Upstream status: spark-ds41f local experiment (PR #1002); not proposed upstream.
